PURPOSE OF v9
This version preserves the institutional architecture of v8 while resolving
four classes of adversarial vulnerability and formal expressiveness:
(1) Preventing retrospective validation loopholes in the Emergency Safe
    Harbor via a Plausibility Pre-Commitment for ad hoc indicators;
(2) Preventing structural gaming of the Cognitive Sovereignty rejection
    metric via a Severity-Weighted Rejection Index;
(3) Eliminating semantic ambiguity in Degraded Mode via a strictly
    bounded sub-optimality constraint (HJB safe envelope);
(4) Closing the pilot-to-production governance gap via a mandatory
    Governance Readiness Level (GRL >= 4) prerequisite for certification;
(5) Expressing the Layered Law of Stop and restart authorities as
    enforceable Linear Temporal Logic (LTL) safety properties.
The operative text is normative. Dated empirical claims and external legal
references belong exclusively to the Explanatory Memorandum.
