ARTICLE 1 - DEFINITIONS AND SYSTEM STATES
1.1  "AI system" means an automated or computational system capable of
generating, ranking, classifying, predicting, recommending, optimizing,
selecting, or otherwise materially influencing information used in a
public decision.
1.2  "Consequential execution" means execution or use of an AI-generated
output in an operational decision capable of producing legal,
administrative, economic, safety, rights-related, or materially
distributive effects.
1.3  "Exploratory simulation" means computational use performed solely for
generation, comparison, testing, or rejection of candidate options,
where no output is used as a consequential operational decision.
1.4  "Problem formulation" means the legally operative definition of:
(a) the administrative or policy problem;
(b) the population, activity, or system within scope;
(c) the operative policy question;
(d) the relevant decision boundary.
1.5  "Priority-setting" means identification of concerns, values, harms,
interests, or questions that citizens consider deserving of
consideration. Priority-setting does not itself constitute legal
problem formulation.
1.6  "Objective-function provenance" means documentation of the values,
priorities, constraints, trade-offs, weights, optimization targets,
proxy variables, and material design choices encoded in an AI system's
objective function or equivalent decision criterion.
1.7  "Safe state" means a technically defined state in which:
(a) no new consequential action is initiated;
(b) relevant system state is preserved for forensic examination;
(c) data and model weights are not intentionally destroyed or altered.
1.8  "Degraded mode" means a restricted operational state permitting only
protective, containment, continuity, or non-expansive functions where
complete cessation would create a greater foreseeable hazard.
1.9  "Emergency Path" means the exceptional regime established by Article 19.
1.10 "Normal Path" means the Article 12 governance cycle applicable outside
a valid Emergency Path declaration.
1.11 "Light Path" means the reduced procedural regime applicable where the
Full-Cycle threshold is not reached and no Emergency Path applies.
