ARTICLE 2 - PATH PRECEDENCE
2.1  Every AI-assisted public decision shall be assigned a legal path before
consequential execution.
2.2  The Emergency Path has precedence over the Normal Path only where all
statutory requirements for an Article 19 emergency declaration are
satisfied.
2.3  A declaration does not itself authorize every form of AI use.
 It authorizes only those emergency uses:
   (a) materially connected to the declared hazard;
   (b) necessary for the declared emergency function;
   (c) within the temporal and substantive limits of Article 19.

2.4  Where Article 19 does not validly apply, the Scope Gate of Article 3
determines whether the matter enters the Full Cycle or Light Path.
2.5  Where an emergency declaration expires, is invalidated, or is withdrawn,
all subsequent consequential execution shall immediately revert to the
applicable Normal-Path requirements unless another lawful authority
independently authorizes the activity.
2.6  An emergency declaration shall not be used to avoid Article 12 where
the factual and temporal conditions of Article 19 are absent.
