ARTICLE 3 - SCOPE GATE
3.1  Two ordinal dimensions shall be assessed:
 Impact Severity I in {1,2,3,4,5}
 Scalability     S in {1,2,3,4,5}

3.2  Impact Severity concerns potential effects upon:
(a) fundamental rights;
(b) physical safety;
(c) economic interests;
(d) access to public services;
(e) materially distributive outcomes.
3.3  Scalability concerns:
(a) population reach;
(b) geographic or institutional reach;
(c) reversibility;
(d) systemic propagation;
(e) dependence of downstream systems.
3.4  Scores are ordinal. No multiplication, averaging, or cardinal
interpretation of I or S is permitted.
3.5  FULL CYCLE applies where ANY of the following conditions is satisfied:
   F = 1 if:
       R = 1
       OR I = 5
       OR S = 5
       OR (I >= 4 AND S >= 4)

 where R = 1 denotes activation of a fundamental-rights trigger.

3.6  LIGHT PATH applies where:
   F = 0
   AND no valid Article 19 emergency exists.

3.7  A fundamental-rights trigger overrides the numerical matrix.
3.8  Where the responsible scorer cannot determine whether a threshold is
satisfied, the higher procedural path shall apply.
3.9  The scorer shall publish:
(a) identity;
(b) I score and reasons;
(c) S score and reasons;
(d) rights-trigger determination;
(e) evidence relied upon.
3.10 The scorer shall be organizationally separate from the project team.
