ARTICLE 4 - SCOPE CHALLENGE AND DEFAULT-UP RULE
4.1  Any natural person, civil-society organization, or parliamentary
minority representing at least 10 percent of the relevant chamber may
challenge a Scope Gate classification within fourteen days.
4.2  The IRA shall decide the challenge within twenty-one days.
4.3  Pending determination, uncertainty shall be resolved upward.
4.4  IRA decisions under this Article remain subject to expedited judicial
review.
4.5  A challenge does not suspend a valid Full-Cycle designation.
4.6  A challenge against a Light-Path designation shall suspend consequential
execution where the petitioner establishes a prima facie possibility
that a Full-Cycle trigger was omitted, unless the court orders otherwise.
