ARTICLE 6 - LIGHT PATH
6.1  A Light-Path matter shall contain:
   (a) a published human-authored framing record;
   (b) at least one rejected alternative;
   (c) a distributive-impact note;
   (d) identification of material AI use;
   (e) objective-function provenance where an AI system is used
       consequentially.

6.2  No mini-public or thirty-day pre-publication delay is required.
6.3  A materially deficient or missing framing record renders the resulting
consequential act subject to the nullity provisions of Article 17.
6.4  Any person may petition the IRA to escalate a Light-Path matter.
6.5  The IRA shall determine an escalation petition within fourteen days.
6.6  Where doubt exists regarding materiality, the higher path applies.
