ARTICLE 7 - ARTICLE 12: NON-DELEGABLE HUMAN FRAMING
7.1  The initial legal formulation of the problem shall be exclusively
human-authored.
7.2  No AI system may:
(a) define the initial problem;
(b) generate the operative problem statement;
(c) narrow the operative policy question;
(d) validate the initial formulation.
7.3  Permitted tooling includes:
(a) search;
(b) translation;
(c) spelling and grammar;
(d) formatting;
(e) accessibility tooling;
 provided that such use is disclosed.

7.4  AI-assisted background research may be used by human authors, but such
use shall not transfer authorship of the legally operative framing.
7.5  Each human author shall file an attestation stating:
   (a) no AI was used to generate, narrow, or validate the operative
       framing;

   (b) any AI used for background research is identified by:
         - provider/tool;
         - version;
         - date;
         - material prompts or queries.

7.6  False attestation constitutes an individual compliance breach and
invalidates the affected framing audit.
