ARTICLE 10 - REGISTRY PUBLICATION AND TEMPORAL GATE
10.1 The completed framing audit shall be published on the Public
Algorithmic Registry.
10.2 Publication shall be:
   (a) machine-readable;
   (b) versioned;
   (c) queryable;
   (d) timestamped;
   (e) cryptographically integrity-protected where technically feasible.

10.3 Publication shall occur at least thirty days before option generation.
10.4 No consequential execution may occur merely because the publication
period has elapsed.
10.5 If two agencies register materially conflicting framings concerning
substantially the same subject matter, the IRA shall publish a
Reconciliation Notice within fourteen days.
10.6 A Reconciliation Notice shall identify:
   (a) the conflicting propositions;
   (b) their scope;
   (c) material normative differences;
   (d) relevant affected populations;
   (e) the legal status of each framing.

10.7 The IRA shall not unilaterally select one agency's substantive policy
preference as legally superior unless authorized by law or judicial
determination.
