ARTICLE 11 - FRAMING-LEVEL DIVERGENCE MATRIX
11.1 Before option generation, the authority shall construct a
Framing-Level Divergence Matrix.
11.2 The matrix shall contain:
   (a) alternative problem framings;
   (b) expected distributive effects;
   (c) dissenting expert annotations;
   (d) material uncertainties;
   (e) unresolved normative disagreements.

11.3 The matrix shall contain NO operational options and NO option families.
11.4 The matrix shall be versioned and published on the Registry.
11.5 Adversarial pluralism applies at the framing level.
11.6 The matrix is a representation of disagreement over problem
constitution, not a mechanism for selecting the final policy.
