ARTICLE 12 - MID-CYCLE MINI-PUBLIC
12.1 A Full-Cycle framing matrix shall be reviewed by an independent
mini-public.
12.2 The mini-public may:
   (a) approve the matrix;
   (b) require amendments;
   (c) reject the matrix with reasons.

12.3 Selection shall use transparent stratified rules.
12.4 A statistically significant deviation from the affected-population
profile shall trigger either:
   (a) automatic re-draw; OR
   (b) a published explanatory addendum establishing why re-draw is not
       feasible and how representativeness is being restored.

12.5 Independent facilitation is mandatory.
12.6 Members receive information rights including:
   (a) the framing audit;
   (b) counter-expertise;
   (c) dissenting briefs;
   (d) read-only real-time telemetry where technically and legally
       appropriate.

12.7 Conflict-of-interest rules apply to members and staff.
12.8 An Affective Dissent Channel shall permit publication of non-deliberative
expressions of refusal, anger, disruption, or dissent.
12.9 Affective dissent shall receive equal publication visibility but shall
remain analytically distinct from reasoned deliberative findings.
12.10 The agency shall issue a written response to material dissent within
fourteen days.
12.11 Where the framing materially burdens a protected group, approval
requires:
   (a) a two-thirds supermajority of the mini-public; AND
   (b) confirmation by the court designated by statute.

12.12 "Protected Group" means:
   (a) a group protected under applicable anti-discrimination law; OR
   (b) a group independently identified by the Accredited Expert Pool
       as bearing a disproportionate burden.

12.13 Rejection shall be reasoned and published.
12.14 Weaponized or unexplained rejection is prohibited.
