ARTICLE 13 - DEADLOCK, SILENCE AND FAST-TRACK
13.1 Administrative silence shall never constitute approval.
13.2 If a mini-public remains silent for forty-five days, the IRA shall
replace the panel by a fresh lot. The statutory review clock then
restarts once.
13.3 A reasoned rejection returns the matter to Article 9.
13.4 After two rejection cycles, an independent IRA Arbitral Panel shall
decide within thirty days.
13.5 The Arbitral Panel shall not be composed of members of the project team,
the rejecting mini-public, or the deploying agency.
13.6 The decision is binding subject to expedited judicial review.
13.7 Fast-track amendments may not:
   (a) change the Primary Problem Statement;
   (b) remove a Rejected Alternative Framing;
   (c) alter a material Distributive Impact conclusion.

13.8 Fast-track amendments shall be separately versioned on the Registry.
