ARTICLE 14 - OPTION GENERATION AND CONSEQUENTIALLY GATED EXECUTION
14.1 Option generation becomes permissible only after approval of the
Framing-Level Divergence Matrix under Article 12.
14.2 Exploratory simulation for option generation is not consequential
execution.
14.3 No exploratory output may be used operationally until the applicable
consequential-execution requirements are satisfied.
14.4 Semantic Sovereignty Metadata shall accompany each consequential model
deployment.
14.5 The metadata shall identify:
   (a) objective-function provenance;
   (b) material normative assumptions;
   (c) affected population;
   (d) decision type;
   (e) data-input classes;
   (f) model version;
   (g) relevant audit identifier.

14.6 A Certificate of Registry Compliance shall be issued by the IRA after
confirmation that Articles 8 through 13 have been completed.
14.7 The certificate is required before consequential model execution.
14.8 No certificate + no valid Article 19 emergency authorization
= no consequential execution.
14.9 The certificate is NOT required for exploratory simulation whose outputs
remain solely within the option-generation process.
14.10 The IRA shall decide a complete certificate application within thirty
days.
14.11 Silence is not approval.
14.12 Where the IRA fails to decide within the statutory period, the applicant
may seek an expedited court order compelling a decision.
14.13 Judicial compulsion to decide does not constitute judicial issuance of
the certificate itself unless the court independently finds that all
statutory requirements are satisfied.

14.14 GOVERNANCE READINESS LEVEL (GRL)
   Before issuing a Certificate of Registry Compliance, the IRA
   shall verify that the deploying agency has achieved a Governance
   Readiness Level (GRL) of at least 4, demonstrating:
   (a) verified statutory funding;
   (b) trained mini-public facilitators;
   (c) successfully completed semi-annual unannounced shadow drills.
