ARTICLE 15 - NORMAL-PATH EX-POST AUDIT
15.1 Within sixty days of deployment, the agency shall publish:
   (a) whether the deployed system matched the approved framing;
   (b) whether it matched the divergence matrix;
   (c) observed distributive impacts;
   (d) predicted-versus-observed differences;
   (e) divergence between pre-registered indicators and actual
       performance;
   (f) lessons for subsequent framing cycles.

15.2 The mini-public validates the audit before the next cycle's framing is
registered.
15.3 Validation constitutes a published finding and not a veto.
15.4 An unresolved adverse finding triggers a new Article 9 audit.
15.5 No ex-post audit may retrospectively legalize an otherwise unauthorized
consequential deployment.
