ARTICLE 19 - ARTICLE 14 EMERGENCY ALGORITHMIC REGIME
19.1 The Emergency Path may be invoked only where an imminent public hazard
or temporal crisis requires action before the Normal Path can reasonably
operate.
19.2 Presumptive hazard classes include:
   (a) public-health emergency;
   (b) armed conflict or imminent security threat;
   (c) systemic financial-stability event;
   (d) critical-infrastructure failure;
   (e) irreversible environmental threshold breach.

19.3 A residual severe and irreversible harm category may be reviewed by
the courts.
19.4 The emergency exception is narrow, temporary, hazard-linked, and
auditable.
19.5 Emergency status does not create general authority over unrelated
AI systems.
