ARTICLE 22 - EMERGENCY LODGING
22.1 The declaration shall be lodged on the Public Algorithmic Registry
within six hours.
22.2 Simultaneous notification shall be made to:
   (a) Parliament;
   (b) National Data Protection Authority;
   (c) Independent Registry Authority.

22.3 Failure to satisfy the six-hour lodging requirement constitutes absolute
legal nullity.
22.4 Late lodging cannot be cured by subsequent audit.
