ARTICLE 41 - JUDICIAL REVIEW
41.1 General expedited review shall cover:
   (a) Scope Gate classifications;
   (b) certificate refusals;
   (c) certificate delays;
   (d) Level 1 and Level 2 IRA orders;
   (e) arbitral-panel decisions;
   (f) refusals to escalate Light-Path matters;
   (g) procedural recalibration decisions.

41.2 The general review period shall be thirty days unless law provides a
shorter emergency period.
41.3 Standing includes applicants, affected persons, CSOs, and parliamentary
minorities meeting the statutory threshold.
41.4 Filing is not suspensory unless the court orders otherwise.
