ARTICLE 42 - EMERGENCY ALGORITHMIC REVIEW BENCH
42.1 A designated High Administrative Court shall possess exclusive
jurisdiction over appeals from L2 regulator-stop orders where emergency
review is required.
42.2 An L2 stop remains operational upon service.
42.3 Appeal does not suspend execution.
42.4 The system remains in safe state or degraded mode during review.
42.5 The accelerated procedure is:
   T + 00h  Service of L2 order
   T + 24h  Filing window closes
   T + 30h  Random selection of technical masters
   T + 36h  Preliminary technical hearing and sandbox access
   T + 72h  Final evidentiary hearing and binding ruling

42.6 Standing includes:
   (a) deploying agency;
   (b) provider;
   (c) persons materially affected by the stop or system.

