ARTICLE 59 - FINAL ANTI-CIRCUMVENTION CLAUSE
59.1 Substance prevails over formal characterization.
59.2 No public authority, provider, or responsible official may obtain
materially greater legal authority merely by:
   (a) renaming a decision;
   (b) dividing a decision;
   (c) distributing a decision among multiple systems;
   (d) sequencing otherwise unified actions;
   (e) converting an operational output into a data-processing step;
   (f) reclassifying an emergency output as ordinary data without
       satisfying Article 33.

59.3 Where multiple actions are materially interdependent, their legal
characterization shall be determined by their substantive relationship.
59.4 The anti-circumvention rule itself remains subject to judicial review.
59.5 Nullity under this Article is subject to the Reliance Rule.
