ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANT
Neither urgency nor audit authority may be captured.
The Emergency Path is a narrow, time-limited, hazard-linked and audited
exception to the Normal Path.
The Law of Stop is institutional rather than merely technical. No single
off-switch is treated as sufficient governance. Authority is distributed
across provider, regulator, infrastructure authority, and judiciary, with
defined safe-state, degraded-mode, restart, and audit procedures.
Algorithmic sovereignty is not equated with national hosting.
The relevant sovereignty question concerns control over:
   objectives,
   provenance,
   decision authority,
   contestability,
   interruption,
   restart,
   and downstream reuse.

The IRA is therefore itself regulated.
The governance regime is also measured against its own claims through
independent auditing, direction-sensitive indicators, published methodology,
and periodic recalibration.
No emergency output becomes legitimate precedent merely through repetition.
No machine-generated premise becomes legally legitimate merely through
repetition.
No procedural metric becomes substantive law merely through administrative
recalibration.
